module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Homology.HomBicomplexSpectralSequences
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cohomology.Acyclicity.TotallyAcyclicSheaves
public import StacksFrontier.Homology.Injectives.FilteredComplex.HomComplex
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The Čech spectral sequence of a locally surjective map of presheaves of sets

Let `𝒞` be a site and let `K' → K` be a map of presheaves of sets whose sheafification is
surjective. Write `K'_p = K' ×_K … ×_K K'` for the fibre power with `p + 1` factors. For every
abelian sheaf `𝓕` there is a cohomological spectral sequence

```
E₁^{p,q} = H^q(K'_p, 𝓕)  ⟹  H^{p+q}(K, 𝓕),
```

which is [Stacks, Tag 079Z].

Here `H^q(K, 𝓕)` is the cohomology of `𝓕` *over the presheaf of sets* `K`, not over an object of
the site: it is the `q`-th right derived functor of `𝓕 ↦ Mor_{PSh(𝒞)}(K, 𝓕)`, computed as `Ext`
out of the free abelian sheaf `ℤ_K^♯` generated by `K`. This is the convention of the section
[Stacks, Tag 079X] and the one
`Stacks.Cohomology.cohomologyOverSheaf` already fixes for a sheaf of sets; the agreement of the
two is `Stacks.Cohomology.cohomologyOverSheafEquivZExt`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Cohomology.cechFibrePower`: the fibre power `K'_p`, a reducible alias for the
  degree-`p` term of Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Arrow.cechNerve`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.cechNerveFreeCochainComplex`: the free abelian sheaf complex of the Čech
  nerve of `K' → K`, read as a cochain complex in the nonpositive degrees.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Cohomology.cohomologyOverSheafEquivZExt`: the cohomology over a sheaf of sets of
  [Stacks, Tag 072Y] is the `ℤ`-graded `Ext` out of the free abelian sheaf, which is the group
  the spectral sequence below is stated with.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.qIsoSingleFreeAbelianSheaf`: the free abelian sheaf complex of the Čech
  nerve represents `ℤ_K^♯` in the derived category. This is [Stacks, Tag 01GC] read as a
  statement about `D(Ab(𝒞))`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi_presheafToSheaf_map`: a map of presheaves of
  sets is locally surjective exactly when its sheafification is surjective.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.exists_firstQuadrant_cechNerveSpectralSequence`: **[Stacks, Tag 079Z]**,
  the first-quadrant spectral sequence with first page `H^q(K'_p, 𝓕)` abutting to
  `H^{p+q}(K, 𝓕)`.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.exists_firstQuadrant_cechNerveSpectralSequence_of_epi_sheafify`: the same,
  with the hypothesis in the source's words.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.exists_abutsTo_cechNerveSpectralSequence` and its `_of_epi_sheafify` form:
  the same spectral sequence without the vanishing of the first page outside the first quadrant.

## Implementation notes

The source proves the lemma by replacing `𝒞` by a larger site on which `K` and `K'` become
objects and `{K' → K}` a covering ([Stacks, Tag 03CI]) and then invoking the Čech-to-cohomology
spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 03AZ]. That route is not taken here, because the library's form of
[Stacks, Tag 03AZ]
(`Stacks.CechSite.exists_cechToCohomology_spectralSequence_sheafCohomologyAbutment`) identifies
the *second* page, as Čech cohomology of the covering family, whereas 079Z asks for the *first*,
whose terms are the cohomology groups of the individual fibre powers. Passing from the former to
the latter would mean reconstructing the double complex the second page was read off from.

Instead the lemma is obtained from the resolution directly. The free abelian sheaves on the terms
of the Čech nerve form a complex which resolves `ℤ_K^♯`: this is [Stacks, Tag 01GC],
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.quasiIso_cechNerveSheafAugmentation`, and it is exactly the hypothesis
of the termwise hyper-`Ext` spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 07AA],
`CochainComplex.exists_termwiseExtSpectralSequence`, whose first page is the `Ext` groups of the
terms of a bounded-above complex and whose abutment is `Ext` out of the complex. Degree `p` of the
Čech nerve is the fibre power with `p + 1` factors, so the first page is `H^q(K'_p, 𝓕)`, and the
resolution identifies the abutment with `H^{p+q}(K, 𝓕)`. The two steps of the source's proof are
thereby replaced by the one input they exist to produce.

The passage from the `ℕ`-indexed chain complex `CategoryTheory.Presheaf` builds to the `ℤ`-indexed
cochain complex [Stacks, Tag 07AA] consumes is extension by zero along
`ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat`, which sends `p` to `-p`; Mathlib's
`HomologicalComplex.quasiIso_extendMap_iff` carries the quasi-isomorphism across and
`HomologicalComplex.extendSingleIso` identifies the extended target as a complex concentrated in
degree zero. No new complex is built.

The hypothesis "the sheafification of `K' → K` is surjective" is carried in two forms. The
spectral sequence is proved with `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective`, which is the
spelling the Čech nerve machinery of this repository already uses and which needs no
sheafification of type-valued presheaves; the source's own form, surjectivity of the
sheafification, is `Stacks.Cohomology.exists_abutsTo_cechNerveSpectralSequence_of_epi_sheafify`,
the two hypotheses being equivalent by
`Stacks.Cohomology.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi_presheafToSheaf_map`.

Functoriality of the spectral sequence in `𝓕` is not asserted, and 079Z does not ask for it; the
spectral sequence comes from [Stacks, Tag 07AA], an existence statement which produces one
spectral sequence per sheaf.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 079Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/079Z)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 079X](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/079X)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01GC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01GC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07AA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07AA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 072Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/072Y)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.Cohomology

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-! ### Cohomology over a presheaf of sets

For a presheaf of sets `K` the group `H^q(K, 𝓕)` is `Ext^q(ℤ_K^♯, 𝓕)`, the derived functor of
`𝓕 ↦ Mor_{PSh(𝒞)}(K, 𝓕)` read through the adjunction between the free abelian sheaf functor and
the underlying presheaf of sets. The spectral sequence below is stated with the `ℤ`-graded
`Abelian.zExt`, which is the grading the hyper-`Ext` machinery uses; this section records that in
the nonnegative degrees it is the group `Stacks.Cohomology.cohomologyOverSheaf` of
[Stacks, Tag 072Y]. -/

/-- **Cohomology over a sheaf of sets is `Ext` out of its free abelian sheaf, in either
grading.** The group `H^p(K, 𝓕)` of [Stacks, Tag 072Y] and the `ℤ`-graded `Ext`-group in which
the Čech spectral sequence below is stated are the same, for `p : ℕ`.

This is Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Abelian.Ext.homEquiv` at the free abelian sheaf on `K`; it is
recorded here because it is what makes the first page and the abutment of
`Stacks.Cohomology.exists_abutsTo_cechNerveSpectralSequence` the cohomology groups
[Stacks, Tag 079Z] names. -/
def cohomologyOverSheafEquivZExt [HasExt.{u + 1} (Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u})]
    (K : Sheaf J (Type u)) (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) (p : ℕ) :
    cohomologyOverSheaf J K F p ≃
      Abelian.zExt ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj K.obj) F (p : ℤ) :=
  Abelian.Ext.homEquiv

variable {K' K : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} (f : K' ⟶ K)

/-- The fibre power `K'_p = K' ×_K … ×_K K'` with `p + 1` factors, as the degree-`p` term of the
Čech nerve of `f`.

This is a reducible alias for Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Arrow.cechNerve`, whose degree-`p` object
is by definition the wide pullback of `p + 1` copies of the source over the target; no second
construction of the fibre powers is made. -/
abbrev cechFibrePower (p : ℕ) : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u :=
  (Arrow.mk f).cechNerve.obj (op (SimplexCategory.mk p))

/-- The complex `s(ℤ_{K'_•}^♯)` of free abelian sheaves on the Čech nerve of `f`, read as a
cochain complex concentrated in the nonpositive degrees: degree `-p` carries `ℤ_{K'_p}^♯`.

It is the complex `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.freeAbelianSheafComplexFunctor` builds,
extended by zero along `ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat`, which is the indexing the termwise
hyper-`Ext` spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 07AA] is stated for. -/
@[sga "4 V 1.10" "special case"]
def cechNerveFreeCochainComplex : CochainComplex (Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) ℤ :=
  ((SimplicialObject.freeAbelianSheafComplexFunctor J).obj
    (Arrow.mk f).cechNerve).extend ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat

/-- The Čech complex is concentrated in the nonpositive degrees. This is Mathlib's instance for
an extension along `ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat`, restated for
`Stacks.Cohomology.cechNerveFreeCochainComplex`, which is a definition and so opaque to instance
search. -/
instance isStrictlyLE_cechNerveFreeCochainComplex :
    CochainComplex.IsStrictlyLE (cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f) 0 :=
  inferInstanceAs (CochainComplex.IsStrictlyLE
    (((SimplicialObject.freeAbelianSheafComplexFunctor J).obj
      (Arrow.mk f).cechNerve).extend ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat) 0)

/-- The Čech complex is bounded above, being concentrated in the nonpositive degrees. -/
lemma minus_cechNerveFreeCochainComplex :
    CochainComplex.minus (Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) (cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f) :=
  ⟨0, inferInstance⟩

/-- Degree `-p` of the Čech complex is the free abelian sheaf on the fibre power `K'_p`. -/
def cechNerveFreeCochainComplexXIso (p : ℕ) :
    (cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f).X (-(p : ℤ)) ≅
      (Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (cechFibrePower f p) :=
  ((SimplicialObject.freeAbelianSheafComplexFunctor J).obj
    (Arrow.mk f).cechNerve).extendXIso ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat (i := p) (by simp)

/-- **The Čech complex of a locally surjective map resolves `ℤ_K^♯`.** In the derived category of
abelian sheaves the complex `s(ℤ_{K'_•}^♯)` is the free abelian sheaf on the target, placed in
degree zero.

This is [Stacks, Tag 01GC], `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.quasiIso_cechNerveSheafAugmentation`,
carried across the extension by zero: a quasi-isomorphism of `ℕ`-indexed complexes extends to one
of `ℤ`-indexed complexes by `HomologicalComplex.quasiIso_extendMap_iff`, the extension of a
complex concentrated in degree zero is again one by `HomologicalComplex.extendSingleIso`, and the
localisation functor inverts quasi-isomorphisms. -/
def qIsoSingleFreeAbelianSheaf (hf : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J f) :
    DerivedCategory.Q.obj (cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f) ≅
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) 0).obj
        ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj K) := by
  have := Presheaf.quasiIso_cechNerveSheafAugmentation J f hf
  have h : IsIso (DerivedCategory.Q.map (HomologicalComplex.extendMap
      (Presheaf.cechNerveSheafAugmentation J f) ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat)) := by
    rw [DerivedCategory.isIso_Q_map_iff_quasiIso]
    infer_instance
  exact (@asIso _ _ _ _ _ h) ≪≫
    DerivedCategory.Q.mapIso
      (HomologicalComplex.extendSingleIso ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat
        ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj K) 0 0 (by simp))

/-- Transporting the first argument of an `Ext`-group along an isomorphism of the derived
category. -/
private def extIsoOfIsoLeft {X Y Z : DerivedCategory (Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u})} (e : X ≅ Y)
    (n : ℤ) :
    AddCommGrpCat.of (DerivedCategory.Ext X Z n) ≅
      AddCommGrpCat.of (DerivedCategory.Ext Y Z n) :=
  (Stacks.Injectives.homCongrAddEquiv e (Iso.refl (Z⟦n⟧))).toAddCommGrpIso

/-- **The Čech spectral sequence, with its first page named in the columns `p ≥ 0`.** Let `𝒞` be
a site and `K' → K` a locally surjective map of presheaves of sets. For every abelian sheaf `𝓕`
there is a cohomological spectral sequence, starting on page one, with

```
E₁^{p,q} = H^q(K'_p, 𝓕),
```

the cohomology of `𝓕` over the fibre power `K'_p = K' ×_K … ×_K K'` with `p + 1` factors,
abutting to `H^{p+q}(K, 𝓕)`.

This statement says nothing about the columns `p < 0` of the first page, so on its own it does not
tie the cohomology of the `K'_p` to that of `K`. The statement of [Stacks, Tag 079Z], which also
asserts that the first page vanishes outside the first quadrant, is
`Stacks.Cohomology.exists_firstQuadrant_cechNerveSpectralSequence`.

Cohomology over a presheaf of sets is `Ext` out of the free abelian sheaf it generates, as in
[Stacks, Tag 072Y]; see `Stacks.Cohomology.cohomologyOverSheafEquivZExt`. Abutment is
`CategoryTheory.SpectralSequence.AbutsTo`: the spectral sequence has an infinity page everywhere
and its terms are the graded pieces of a finite decreasing filtration of each `H^n(K, 𝓕)`. -/
theorem exists_abutsTo_cechNerveSpectralSequence (hf : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J f)
    (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) :
    ∃ E : CohomologicalSpectralSequence AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} 1,
      (∀ (p : ℕ) (q : ℤ), Nonempty ((E.page 1).X ((p : ℤ), q) ≅
        AddCommGrpCat.of (Abelian.zExt
          ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (cechFibrePower f p)) F q))) ∧
      SpectralSequence.AbutsTo E (fun n ↦ AddCommGrpCat.of
        (Abelian.zExt ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj K) F n)) := by
  obtain ⟨E, hE₁, habuts⟩ := CochainComplex.exists_termwiseExtSpectralSequence
    (cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f) (minus_cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f) F
  refine ⟨E, fun p q ↦ ?_, habuts.of_iso fun n ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact ⟨(hE₁ (p : ℤ) q).some ≪≫
      extIsoOfIsoLeft J ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor _ 0).mapIso
        (cechNerveFreeCochainComplexXIso J f p)) q⟩
  · exact extIsoOfIsoLeft J (qIsoSingleFreeAbelianSheaf J f hf) n

omit [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] in
/-- **A map of presheaves of sets is locally surjective exactly when its sheafification is
surjective.** This identifies the hypothesis of
`Stacks.Cohomology.exists_abutsTo_cechNerveSpectralSequence` with the one
[Stacks, Tag 079Z] states, surjectivity being epimorphy of sheaves.

The argument is the one `CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.WEqualsLocallyBijective.mk'` makes
for local bijectivity: local surjectivity of `f` is unchanged by composing with the locally
bijective unit `K ⟶ K^♯`, and that composite is the sheafification of `f` precomposed with the
unit at the source. -/
@[sga "3 IV 6.7.3" "more general", sga "3 VIB 10.15" "more general"]
lemma isLocallySurjective_iff_epi_presheafToSheaf_map [HasSheafify J (Type u)] :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J f ↔ Epi ((presheafToSheaf J (Type u)).map f) := by
  rw [← Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi,
    ← Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_comp_iff J f (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J K),
    CategoryTheory.toSheafify_naturality, Presheaf.comp_isLocallySurjective_iff]

/-- **The Čech spectral sequence, with its first page named in the columns `p ≥ 0`**, with the
hypothesis in the source's words: the sheafification of `K' → K` is surjective, i.e. an
epimorphism of sheaves of sets.

This is `Stacks.Cohomology.exists_abutsTo_cechNerveSpectralSequence` read through
`Stacks.Cohomology.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi_presheafToSheaf_map`. Like that statement it says
nothing about the columns `p < 0`; the full statement of [Stacks, Tag 079Z] is
`Stacks.Cohomology.exists_firstQuadrant_cechNerveSpectralSequence_of_epi_sheafify`. -/
theorem exists_abutsTo_cechNerveSpectralSequence_of_epi_sheafify [HasSheafify J (Type u)]
    (hf : Epi ((presheafToSheaf J (Type u)).map f)) (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) :
    ∃ E : CohomologicalSpectralSequence AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} 1,
      (∀ (p : ℕ) (q : ℤ), Nonempty ((E.page 1).X ((p : ℤ), q) ≅
        AddCommGrpCat.of (Abelian.zExt
          ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (cechFibrePower f p)) F q))) ∧
      SpectralSequence.AbutsTo E (fun n ↦ AddCommGrpCat.of
        (Abelian.zExt ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj K) F n)) :=
  exists_abutsTo_cechNerveSpectralSequence J f
    ((isLocallySurjective_iff_epi_presheafToSheaf_map J f).2 hf) F

/-- The first page of the termwise `Ext` spectral sequence of the Čech complex vanishes outside
the first quadrant: in a column `p < 0` the term of the Čech complex is zero, and in a row
`q < 0` the `Ext`-group between two sheaves is zero. -/
private lemma isZero_zExt_cechNerveFreeCochainComplex_X (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u})
    (p q : ℤ) (hpq : p < 0 ∨ q < 0) :
    IsZero (AddCommGrpCat.of (Abelian.zExt ((cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f).X (-p)) F q)) := by
  have : Subsingleton (Abelian.zExt ((cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f).X (-p)) F q) := by
    refine subsingleton_of_forall_eq 0 fun g => ?_
    rcases hpq with hp | hq
    · have hterm : IsZero ((cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f).X (-p)) :=
        (cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f).isZero_of_isStrictlyLE 0 (-p) (by omega)
      exact (Functor.map_isZero (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor _ 0) hterm).eq_of_src _ _
    · have hbij := DerivedCategory.bijective_homologyFunctor_shiftMap_of_isLE_of_isGE
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) 0).obj
          ((cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f).X (-p)))
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) 0).obj F) 0 0 q q
        (by omega) (by omega)
      have hzero : IsZero ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) q).obj
          ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) 0).obj F)) :=
        DerivedCategory.isZero_of_isGE _ 0 q (by omega)
      exact hbij.1 (hzero.eq_of_tgt _ _)
  exact AddCommGrpCat.isZero_of_subsingleton _

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 079Z.** Let `𝒞` be a site and `K' → K` a map of presheaves of sets
whose sheafification is surjective (here: which is locally surjective, the same condition by
`Stacks.Cohomology.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi_presheafToSheaf_map`). For every abelian sheaf `𝓕`
there is a first-quadrant cohomological spectral sequence, starting on page one, with

```
E₁^{p,q} = H^q(K'_p, 𝓕)   (p ≥ 0),    E₁^{p,q} = 0   (p < 0 or q < 0),
```

where `K'_p = K' ×_K … ×_K K'` is the fibre power with `p + 1` factors, abutting to
`H^{p+q}(K, 𝓕)`.

Cohomology over a presheaf of sets is `Ext` out of the free abelian sheaf it generates, as in
[Stacks, Tag 079X] and [Stacks, Tag 072Y]; see `Stacks.Cohomology.cohomologyOverSheafEquivZExt`.
Abutment is `CategoryTheory.SpectralSequence.AbutsTo`: the spectral sequence has an infinity page
everywhere and its terms are the graded pieces of a finite decreasing filtration of each
`H^n(K, 𝓕)`. -/
@[stacks 079Z]
theorem exists_firstQuadrant_cechNerveSpectralSequence (hf : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J f)
    (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) :
    ∃ E : CohomologicalSpectralSequence AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} 1,
      (∀ (p : ℕ) (q : ℤ), Nonempty ((E.page 1).X ((p : ℤ), q) ≅
        AddCommGrpCat.of (Abelian.zExt
          ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (cechFibrePower f p)) F q))) ∧
      (∀ p q : ℤ, p < 0 ∨ q < 0 → IsZero ((E.page 1).X (p, q))) ∧
      SpectralSequence.AbutsTo E (fun n ↦ AddCommGrpCat.of
        (Abelian.zExt ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj K) F n)) := by
  obtain ⟨E, hE₁, habuts⟩ := CochainComplex.exists_termwiseExtSpectralSequence
    (cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f) (minus_cechNerveFreeCochainComplex J f) F
  refine ⟨E, fun p q ↦ ?_, fun p q hpq ↦ ?_, habuts.of_iso fun n ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact ⟨(hE₁ (p : ℤ) q).some ≪≫
      extIsoOfIsoLeft J ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor _ 0).mapIso
        (cechNerveFreeCochainComplexXIso J f p)) q⟩
  · exact (isZero_zExt_cechNerveFreeCochainComplex_X J f F p q hpq).of_iso (hE₁ p q).some
  · exact extIsoOfIsoLeft J (qIsoSingleFreeAbelianSheaf J f hf) n

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 079Z**, with the hypothesis in the source's own words: if the
sheafification of `K' → K` is surjective, i.e. an epimorphism of sheaves of sets, then for every
abelian sheaf `𝓕` there is a first-quadrant spectral sequence with `E₁^{p,q} = H^q(K'_p, 𝓕)` for
`p ≥ 0`, `E₁^{p,q} = 0` for `p < 0` or `q < 0`, abutting to `H^{p+q}(K, 𝓕)`.

This is `Stacks.Cohomology.exists_firstQuadrant_cechNerveSpectralSequence` read through
`Stacks.Cohomology.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi_presheafToSheaf_map`. -/
@[stacks 079Z]
theorem exists_firstQuadrant_cechNerveSpectralSequence_of_epi_sheafify [HasSheafify J (Type u)]
    (hf : Epi ((presheafToSheaf J (Type u)).map f)) (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u}) :
    ∃ E : CohomologicalSpectralSequence AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1} 1,
      (∀ (p : ℕ) (q : ℤ), Nonempty ((E.page 1).X ((p : ℤ), q) ≅
        AddCommGrpCat.of (Abelian.zExt
          ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj (cechFibrePower f p)) F q))) ∧
      (∀ p q : ℤ, p < 0 ∨ q < 0 → IsZero ((E.page 1).X (p, q))) ∧
      SpectralSequence.AbutsTo E (fun n ↦ AddCommGrpCat.of
        (Abelian.zExt ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj K) F n)) :=
  exists_firstQuadrant_cechNerveSpectralSequence J f
    ((isLocallySurjective_iff_epi_presheafToSheaf_map J f).2 hf) F

end Stacks.Cohomology

end
